id: pm-memory-recall-freshness
title: Report stale or contradictory knowledge in task recall
description: "Reuse existing verification and supersession signals to expose bounded, checkable freshness and contradiction evidence during task recall."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-11-19T06:08:31.207Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-19T15:05:08.554Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: Agents can recover source evidence for a disclosed conflict without reading every candidate.
parent: pm-memory-0kwy
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-19T14:01:30.994Z",codex-sol,"Design: expose evidence through an opt-in SDK resume intent. Use a certified same-tracker snapshot, persist no recall exposure, keep complete rows within the existing ceiling, and report omitted rows and conflict evidence. Reuse native verification and supersession; disclose a single-field source only when it can adjudicate the competing guidance."
  "2026-11-19T14:11:40.400Z",codex-sol,"Scratch copy of the public tracker, with public facts and a synthetic recorded contradiction: resume plus both status, updated_at and dependencies reads took 262 TOON tokens (100 + 69 + 93). Resume-evidence plus the named dependencies read took 233 (155 + 78), saving 29 tokens and one read. The dependencies-only baseline with native ids supplied tied at 233. Counts use the SDK UTF-8 byte estimator."
  "2026-11-19T14:20:58.607Z",codex-sol,The pinned SDK stores a forward supersedes relationship. Resume-evidence derives the incoming superseded side and identifies the item that owns the edge. Explicit opposing guidance can use a persisted stale reason. Reciprocal edges and opposing guidance without a decisive source produce a conflict_sources receipt. Local targeted recall tests passed; the legacy missing-field branch has a dedicated fixture under verification.
  "2026-11-19T14:46:40.418Z",codex-sol,"Stock origin/main and candidate resume output matched byte-for-byte on the scratch tracker. Reading the conflict-returned source and field reproduced the named projection. Direct npm run test:install hit the 30-minute install.acceptance.ts file watchdog during the packed Bun fixture. Reference-suffix consumers and shipped-files checks passed. The unchanged install suite is running with PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE=3."
  "2026-11-19T15:05:07.616Z",codex-sol,"Implementation 3750d2ba92fcb8af2bedd74dd462143ad8f5945d. Typecheck, lint, identity, duplication, docstrings and regenerated changelog check passed. All four recall cases passed with 100% statements, branches, functions and lines for src/task-recall.ts. PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE=3 npm run test:install passed all four packed npm/Bun and publishing-file checks. The full quick coverage command reported a failure in the existing 1 MiB policy-framing case. That case passed on stock main and this branch in isolation, and again on this branch with V8 coverage instrumentation. The full local run is still collecting results; exact-head GitHub checks are pending."
files[4]{path,scope}:
  index.ts,project
  src/commands.ts,project
  src/task-recall.ts,project
  test/task-recall.test.ts,project
tests[6]{command,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
  npm run typecheck && npm run lint,project,codex-sol,"2026-11-19T14:10:36.014Z",local_mutation,feat/recall-freshness
  PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE=3 node --import ./test/support/file-deadline.ts --test --test-reporter=tap test/task-recall.test.ts,project,codex-sol,"2026-11-19T14:10:49.744Z",local_mutation,feat/recall-freshness
  PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE=3 npm run coverage,project,codex-sol,"2026-11-19T14:11:04.446Z",local_mutation,feat/recall-freshness
  "npm run test:install",project,codex-sol,"2026-11-19T14:11:15.631Z",local_mutation,feat/recall-freshness
  "git fetch --tags origin && npm run changelog:full && npm run changelog:check",project,codex-sol,"2026-11-19T14:11:28.942Z",local_mutation,feat/recall-freshness
  "PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE=3 npm run test:install",project,codex-sol,"2026-11-19T14:36:30.057Z",local_mutation,feat/recall-freshness
docs[1]{path,scope}:
  README.md,project
